{"qid": "Q0255", "answer": "Based on the company history and timeline, the milestone \"Reorganisation Keel announced: 68 roles eliminated\" is dated **17 August 2022** [1, 6].", "abstained": false, "refused": false, "clarified": false, "sources": ["LS-HIS-2026-0002", "LS-CLS-2023-0002", "LS-HBK-2026-0001", "LS-INV-2023-0001", "LS-MEM-2022-0006", "LS-HIS-2026-0001", "LS-DCH-2026-0022"], "route": "vanilla", "route_used": "vanilla", "graph_rows": 0, "graph_attempted": false, "graph_error": null, "graph_cypher": null, "graph_linked": null, "graph_facts": [], "seconds": 9.67, "llm_calls": 2, "error": null}
{"qid": "Q0256", "answer": "Based on the provided sources, the milestone for migrating HR records to PeopleHub (listed as part of Milestone M5: Analytics & AI function live; PeopleHub and payroll cut-over) is dated **1 October 2019** [1].", "abstained": false, "refused": false, "clarified": false, "sources": ["LS-MNA-2019-0001", "LS-DCH-2026-0025", "LS-SOP-2026-0001", "LS-POL-2025-0006", "LS-HBK-2026-0001", "LS-POL-2026-0008"], "route": "vanilla", "route_used": "vanilla", "graph_rows": 0, "graph_attempted": false, "graph_error": null, "graph_cypher": null, "graph_linked": null, "graph_facts": [], "seconds": 6.51, "llm_calls": 2, "error": null}
{"qid": "Q0278", "answer": "Based on the 2026 employee handbook [1], the details regarding creche support and reimbursement are as follows:\n\n* **Eligibility:** Available to every parent regardless of gender, as well as adoptive parents, for children below the age of six [1]. \n* **Reimbursement Amount:** Lumenstack reimburses creche or day-care fees of up to **₹8,000 per month per child** until the child turns six [1]. The cap applies per child per month, meaning any unused amount for one child cannot be transferred to another [3].\n* **Requirements:** The creche must be a registered facility that issues receipts; payments made to individual nannies or family members are not covered [1].\n* **How to Claim:** Submit the monthly receipt in LedgerOne under the category \"Creche reimbursement\" [1]. Approved claims are paid with your next salary [1].", "abstained": false, "refused": false, "clarified": false, "sources": ["LS-HBK-2026-0001"], "route": "vanilla", "route_used": "vanilla", "graph_rows": 0, "graph_attempted": false, "graph_error": null, "graph_cypher": null, "graph_linked": null, "graph_facts": [], "seconds": 6.14, "llm_calls": 2, "error": null}
{"qid": "Q0280", "answer": "Based on the 2026 employee handbook, the rules regarding **marriage leave** are:\n\n* **Entitlement:** You may take 3 working days of marriage leave once during your employment with Lumenstack for your own wedding [14].\n* **Combining leave:** It can be combined with Earned Leave (making it a rare exception to the usual stacking rules, as weddings in the region tend to take longer than a weekend) [14].\n* **Application:** You must apply at least two weeks in advance [14].", "abstained": false, "refused": false, "clarified": false, "sources": ["LS-HBK-2026-0001", "LS-POL-2026-0008"], "route": "vanilla", "route_used": "vanilla", "graph_rows": 0, "graph_attempted": false, "graph_error": null, "graph_cypher": null, "graph_linked": null, "graph_facts": [], "seconds": 6.15, "llm_calls": 2, "error": null}
{"qid": "Q0282", "answer": "Based on the 2026 employee handbook, the home-internet allowance is handled as follows:\n\n* **In India:** Every full-time employee receives a home-internet allowance of ₹1,500 per month, which is paid with their salary as part of monthly payroll [2]. \n* **Receipts:** Employees do not need to submit bills for it, and it appears as a separate line on their payslip [2].\n* **Outside India:** Colleagues outside India receive equivalent support as described in their country annexures [2].\n* **Taxability:** It is treated according to the income-tax rules that apply to the employee, with the tax treatment handled by Ledgerline Payroll Services and reflected on the payslip [1].", "abstained": false, "refused": false, "clarified": false, "sources": ["LS-HBK-2026-0001"], "route": "vanilla", "route_used": "vanilla", "graph_rows": 0, "graph_attempted": false, "graph_error": null, "graph_cypher": null, "graph_linked": null, "graph_facts": [], "seconds": 7.15, "llm_calls": 2, "error": null}
{"qid": "Q0284", "answer": "Based on the provided employee handbook, Lumen Points cannot be paid out as cash in your settlement upon leaving [2]. You must redeem them before your last day through the rewards portal [2].", "abstained": false, "refused": false, "clarified": false, "sources": ["LS-HBK-2026-0001", "LS-NWS-2026-0005", "LS-NWS-2026-0004", "LS-DEI-2026-0001", "LS-ESG-2026-0001"], "route": "vanilla", "route_used": "vanilla", "graph_rows": 0, "graph_attempted": false, "graph_error": null, "graph_cypher": null, "graph_linked": null, "graph_facts": [], "seconds": 5.13, "llm_calls": 2, "error": null}
{"qid": "Q0288", "answer": "Based on the 2026 Employee Handbook (and related office guides included in the sources), wellness rooms are mentioned in the context of office facilities and employee support:\n\n* **Hyderabad Headquarters (Lumen House):** There is a wellness room on the ground floor that can be booked in 30-minute slots through the room-booking system [6]. It is described as a quiet space with soft lighting, a reclining chair, and no screens for anyone who needs a pause (such as for a migraine, a difficult phone call, prayer, or ten minutes of quiet) [6]. Nursing mothers have priority access, and a separate lactation room with a refrigerator is available on the second floor [6]. Users are asked not to use it for calls or stay longer than their booking [6].\n* **Bengaluru Office (Orbit Tech Park):** A first-aid room and a wellness room are located on the ground floor [7].", "abstained": false, "refused": false, "clarified": false, "sources": ["LS-HBK-2026-0001", "LS-OFG-2026-0002"], "route": "vanilla", "route_used": "vanilla", "graph_rows": 0, "graph_attempted": false, "graph_error": null, "graph_cypher": null, "graph_linked": null, "graph_facts": [], "seconds": 6.32, "llm_calls": 2, "error": null}
