{"qid": "Q1000", "answer": "According to the Design department charter's leadership history, **Vidya Arora** became head of the department (with the title Director, Design) on 19 March 2019 [1].", "abstained": false, "refused": false, "clarified": false, "sources": ["LS-DCH-2026-0010", "LS-DCH-2026-0022", "LS-DCH-2026-0009", "LS-DCH-2026-0005", "LS-DCH-2026-0001", "LS-DCH-2026-0002", "LS-DCH-2026-0023", "LS-DCH-2026-0018"], "route": "vanilla", "route_used": "vanilla", "graph_rows": 0, "graph_attempted": false, "graph_error": null, "graph_cypher": null, "graph_linked": null, "graph_facts": [], "seconds": 44.68, "llm_calls": 2, "error": null}
{"qid": "Q1012", "answer": "According to the Security Engineering department charter, Nikhil Bhatt became head of the department (serving as Senior Manager, Security Engineering) on 1 February 2022 [1].", "abstained": false, "refused": false, "clarified": false, "sources": ["LS-DCH-2026-0008", "LS-DCH-2026-0007", "LS-DCH-2026-0001", "LS-HIS-2026-0002", "LS-DCH-2026-0024", "LS-DCH-2026-0005", "LS-DCH-2026-0027", "LS-DCH-2026-0023"], "route": "vanilla", "route_used": "vanilla", "graph_rows": 0, "graph_attempted": false, "graph_error": null, "graph_cypher": null, "graph_linked": null, "graph_facts": [], "seconds": 51.44, "llm_calls": 2, "error": null}
{"qid": "Q1018", "answer": "According to the leadership history in the Corporate IT department charter, **Prasad Kolluri** became Director IT on 1 April 2020 (having previously served as Head of IT from 2017-05-02 to 2020-03-31) [6].", "abstained": false, "refused": false, "clarified": false, "sources": ["LS-DCH-2026-0007", "LS-DCH-2026-0003", "LS-DCH-2026-0021", "LS-DCH-2026-0018", "LS-DCH-2026-0020", "LS-DCH-2026-0014", "LS-DCH-2026-0001", "LS-DCH-2026-0005"], "route": "vanilla", "route_used": "vanilla", "graph_rows": 0, "graph_attempted": false, "graph_error": null, "graph_cypher": null, "graph_linked": null, "graph_facts": [], "seconds": 52.66, "llm_calls": 2, "error": null}
{"qid": "Q1030", "answer": "Under the Travel and Expense Policy (v3.0, effective 1 April 2019), the domestic per diem allowance on 30 September 2019 was **₹1,000 per day** [5, 8].", "abstained": false, "refused": false, "clarified": false, "sources": ["LS-POL-2022-0003", "LS-POL-2024-0003", "LS-POL-2026-0010", "LS-FAQ-2024-0001", "LS-POL-2019-0002", "LS-POL-2016-0004"], "route": "vanilla", "route_used": "vanilla", "graph_rows": 0, "graph_attempted": false, "graph_error": null, "graph_cypher": null, "graph_linked": null, "graph_facts": [], "seconds": 48.39, "llm_calls": 2, "error": null}
{"qid": "Q1037", "answer": "On 31 December 2015, the employee stock option plan pool percentage was 8 per cent under Version 1.0 of the Employee Stock Option Plan (POL-FIN-005) [1, 2].", "abstained": false, "refused": false, "clarified": false, "sources": ["LS-POL-2018-0005", "LS-POL-2015-0001", "LS-POL-2025-0004", "LS-HBK-2026-0001", "LS-PRS-2015-0001", "LS-CAP-2025-0001", "LS-CAP-2021-0001"], "route": "vanilla", "route_used": "vanilla", "graph_rows": 0, "graph_attempted": false, "graph_error": null, "graph_cypher": null, "graph_linked": null, "graph_facts": [], "seconds": 38.47, "llm_calls": 2, "error": null}
{"qid": "Q1038", "answer": "When version 2.0 replaced version 1.0 of the Employee Stock Option Plan, the option pool percentage increased by **2 percentage points** (from 8% to 10%) [9, 11]. \n\n* **Old value (Version 1.0):** 8% [13]\n* **New value (Version 2.0):** 10% [9]", "abstained": false, "refused": false, "clarified": false, "sources": ["LS-POL-2018-0005", "LS-POL-2015-0001", "LS-POL-2025-0004", "LS-HBK-2026-0001", "LS-CAP-2021-0001", "LS-CAP-2024-0001", "LS-CAP-2025-0001", "LS-POL-2018-0004"], "route": "vanilla", "route_used": "vanilla", "graph_rows": 0, "graph_attempted": false, "graph_error": null, "graph_cypher": null, "graph_linked": null, "graph_facts": [], "seconds": 44.99, "llm_calls": 2, "error": null}
{"qid": "Q1041", "answer": "When version 4.0 replaced version 3.0 of the Code of Conduct, the values count changed from **6 to 5** (a decrease of 1) [9]. \n\n* **Old count / values (Version 3.0):** 6 values (the pre-2021 list included \"Frugal by default\" as the sixth value alongside the current five) [2, 4].\n* **New count / values (Version 4.0):** 5 values (Customers see the light first, Own the outcome, Candour with care, Build to last, Learn out loud) [2, 4, 10].", "abstained": false, "refused": false, "clarified": false, "sources": ["LS-POL-2023-0003", "LS-HBK-2026-0001", "LS-PMR-2022-0009", "LS-MEM-2021-0012", "LS-POL-2023-0006", "LS-POL-2026-0015", "LS-RES-2023-0001", "LS-POL-2022-0008"], "route": "vanilla", "route_used": "vanilla", "graph_rows": 0, "graph_attempted": false, "graph_error": null, "graph_cypher": null, "graph_linked": null, "graph_facts": [], "seconds": 40.71, "llm_calls": 2, "error": null}
{"qid": "Q1042", "answer": "Based on the revision history of the Leave Policy (POL-HR-003):\n\n* **Earned leave days on 30 September 2015:** **20 working days** (effective from 1 April 2018, version 3.0) [2]. \n  * *Note:* Version 2.0 (effective 1 April 2015) updated sick, casual, and paternity leave, but did not change earned leave [2]. Earned leave was set to 20 days in version 3.0 (effective 1 April 2018) [2], and earlier records show it was lower (18 days under version 3.0, and presumably 18 or fewer before that) [2].", "abstained": false, "refused": false, "clarified": false, "sources": ["LS-MEM-2026-0016", "LS-POL-2026-0008", "LS-POL-2026-0009", "LS-HBK-2026-0001", "LS-DCH-2026-0025", "LS-MEM-2026-0017", "LS-FAQ-2025-0001"], "route": "vanilla", "route_used": "vanilla", "graph_rows": 0, "graph_attempted": false, "graph_error": null, "graph_cypher": null, "graph_linked": null, "graph_facts": [], "seconds": 16.6, "llm_calls": 2, "error": null}
